; examples/syntax-quote.nx — syntax-quote, unquote, splicing, gensym.
;
; Demonstrates the macro author's primary tool. The runtime
; constructs lists, splices in computed lists, and auto-gensyms
; hygenic names — all without any stdlib.

(def parts (quote (b c d)))

; Splice parts into the middle of a quoted list. The ~@ form
; spreads the elements of `parts` inline; bracketing `a` and `e`
; are literal symbols, qualified to the current namespace the
; way Clojure's syntax-quote does.
`(a ~@parts e)
; => (user/a b c d user/e)
